course: dictionary
lesson: 7911
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. The word rattle is a good example. «A cobra spreads its hood, a rattlesnake buzzes its rattle» is about a sound, but «the Rat rattles off a huge list of food» is about saying things quickly.
explain: Look at the words around it first. In «windows rattle in the wind», the wind is the clue: the windows make short knocking sounds as they shake. If someone is «rattled», the sentence will usually show they feel nervous. Read the whole sentence before you choose a meaning.
explain: Test your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you probably have it right. If it does not, try another meaning. When context is not enough, check a dictionary.
fact: Rattle can be a verb (to rattle, rattles, rattled) or a noun (a rattle, rattles).
fact: «Rattle» means to make a lot of short knocking sounds by shaking, or to shake something so it does this.
fact: «A rattle» is a baby's toy that makes a noise when shaken.
fact: «To rattle someone» means to make them nervous, and «to rattle off» means to say a list quickly.
fact: A rattlesnake's rattle is the end of its tail, and the snake shakes it as a warning.
exercise: «The Rat rattles off a huge list of food all in one breath.» What does rattles off mean here? | To lose the list | *To say the list quickly | To write the list slowly | To shake the list
exercise: «Windows rattle in the wind.» What are the windows doing? | They are moving very slowly | They are broken forever | *They make short knocking sounds as they shake | They are painted and closed
exercise: «The baby shook her rattle and laughed.» What is a rattle in this sentence? | A cup for milk | A kind of bird | A loud horn | *A toy that makes a noise when shaken
test: «The loud news rattled him, and he could not sit still.» What does rattled mean? | Made him sleepy | *Made him nervous | Made him hungry | Made him wet
test: «A rattlesnake buzzes its rattle.» What is the rattle used for? | To keep the snake warm | To catch food | To sing to its friends | *To warn that it is dangerous
exam: «A porcupine rattles its quills and stamps its feet as a warning first.» What does rattles mean here? | To sleep quietly | To hide from the attacker | *To shake, making short knocking sounds, as a warning | To sing softly
